WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.876 --> 00:00:15.944
Wukong landed on Mount Potalaka.

2
00:00:17.064 --> 00:00:18.985
A young man was meditating in the garden.

3
00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:20.986
"Where's Guanyin?"

4
00:00:21.246 --> 00:00:21.867
asked the monkey.

5
00:00:22.847 --> 00:00:24.668
making a basket," said the man.

6
00:00:25.749 --> 00:00:27.049
He glanced up at the monkey.

7
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:29.431
"It's good to see you again, Wukong."

8
00:00:30.892 --> 00:00:31.472
was puzzled.

9
00:00:32.104 --> 00:00:33.365
"How do you know my name?"

10
00:00:33.445 --> 00:00:35.465
"Don't you recognize me?"

11
00:00:35.726 --> 00:00:36.346
said the man.

12
00:00:39.047 --> 00:00:41.468
Wukong stared for a moment and then gasped.

13
00:00:42.828 --> 00:00:43.469
Red Boy!

14
00:00:44.349 --> 00:00:45.850
You look like a kind spirit now."

15
00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.431
said Red Boy.

16
00:00:48.451 --> 00:00:50.792
"I'm not an evil demon anymore.

17
00:00:51.892 --> 00:00:53.212
I have you to thank for that.

18
00:00:53.993 --> 00:00:55.253
You brought Guanyin to me.

19
00:00:56.054 --> 00:00:59.535
She has taught me all about Buddhism, and now I'm very happy."

20
00:01:00.475 --> 00:01:01.776
welcome," said Wukong.

21
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:04.361
"You and I have a lot in common.

22
00:01:05.161 --> 00:01:07.702
were both evil, causing all sorts of problems.

23
00:01:08.963 --> 00:01:09.923
Now we're both Buddhists."

24
00:01:12.464 --> 00:01:13.945
came over holding a basket.

25
00:01:13.965 --> 00:01:17.066
"Hello, Wukong," said the bodhisattva.

26
00:01:17.986 --> 00:01:19.587
"I knew you would come here today.

27
00:01:20.407 --> 00:01:22.668
I've been working on this basket all morning."

28
00:01:24.569 --> 00:01:27.310
A look of confusion spread across the monkey's face.

29
00:01:28.731 --> 00:01:31.012
a nice basket, Bodhisattva.

30
00:01:31.744 --> 00:01:33.425
But what is it for?"

31
00:01:33.505 --> 00:01:37.908
"This basket has magical powers," said Guanyin.

32
00:01:37.928 --> 00:01:40.310
"I will catch the demon with it.

33
00:01:41.271 --> 00:01:41.791
Let's go."

34
00:01:49.937 --> 00:01:52.138
Wukong returned to the river with Guanyin.

35
00:01:53.059 --> 00:01:56.641
The bodhisattva used a rope to lower the basket into the river.

36
00:01:58.142 --> 00:02:00.244
She recited a spell and then waited.

37
00:02:01.712 --> 00:02:04.794
After a moment she pulled the basket out of the water.

38
00:02:09.837 --> 00:02:10.757
looked in the basket.

39
00:02:11.638 --> 00:02:15.440
A small goldfish was flopping around in it.

40
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:16.841
The monkey laughed.

41
00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.862
guess you need to try again, Bodhisattva.

42
00:02:20.823 --> 00:02:22.124
That's not the demon."

43
00:02:23.585 --> 00:02:25.626
is my goldfish," said Guanyin.

44
00:02:25.646 --> 00:02:30.308
"It usually lives in my lotus pond.

45
00:02:30.368 --> 00:02:33.389
The pond is near my garden, where I teach my students.

46
00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:38.472
After years of listening to my lessons, the fish became a spirit.

47
00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.833
escaped to Earth a few days ago.

48
00:02:42.694 --> 00:02:44.254
I had been wondering where it was."

49
00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:47.816
"A few days ago," repeated Wukong.

50
00:02:47.836 --> 00:02:51.438
"That means it's been on Earth for a few years."

51
00:02:53.318 --> 00:02:54.059
said Guanyin.

52
00:02:54.879 --> 00:02:57.104
"The Tang Monk is safe now.

53
00:02:57.184 --> 00:03:01.568
You may go free him and continue your journey to the Western Paradise."

54
00:03:02.629 --> 00:03:06.592
Guanyin flew off, and Wukong swam down to the palace.

55
00:03:09.154 --> 00:03:12.217
Now that the goldfish was gone, so was its magic.

56
00:03:12.937 --> 00:03:16.660
The monkey smashed the rocks with his iron bar and went inside.

57
00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.162
"Master, I'm here!"

58
00:03:19.503 --> 00:03:20.023
he cried.

59
00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:25.688
He got the monk out of the box and carried him out of the river.

60
00:03:27.648 --> 00:03:31.769
By now all the villagers had heard that Wukong had saved Chen's son.

61
00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.750
When the travelers returned, the villagers cheered.

62
00:03:44.373 --> 00:03:45.813
stay in our village!"

63
00:03:46.173 --> 00:03:46.913
said a man.

64
00:03:46.933 --> 00:03:49.774
"Yes," said an old woman.

65
00:03:51.055 --> 00:03:52.615
no rush to leave.

66
00:03:53.575 --> 00:03:56.964
Stay for as long as you like."

67
00:03:57.044 --> 00:03:58.545
"Thank you," said the Tang Monk.

68
00:03:58.565 --> 00:04:01.287
"But we can stay only one more night, to rest.

69
00:04:02.268 --> 00:04:03.329
the morning we must leave.

70
00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:05.631
We still have far to travel."

71
00:04:07.892 --> 00:04:10.654
The villagers held a feast for the travelers that evening.

72
00:04:12.276 --> 00:04:14.777
By the time everyone went to sleep, it was late.

73
00:04:17.479 --> 00:04:20.362
The next morning the travelers woke to the sound of chopping.

74
00:04:20.382 --> 00:04:22.063
"What's going on?"

75
00:04:22.403 --> 00:04:23.344
asked the Tang Monk.

76
00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.322
They went to the river and found a very busy scene.

77
00:04:29.044 --> 00:04:30.685
men were chopping down trees.

78
00:04:31.986 --> 00:04:33.387
Other people carried tools.

79
00:04:34.548 --> 00:04:36.169
"We're building a boat for you!"

80
00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:37.731
said a smiling man.

81
00:04:37.751 --> 00:04:40.133
"Thank you," said the monk.

82
00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:43.976
He and his companions sat down by the water to wait.

83
00:04:45.177 --> 00:04:48.740
Suddenly there was a rumble, and waves splashed onto the shore.

84
00:04:50.077 --> 00:04:54.333
Everyone stared in fear as a large creature rose from the waves.
